            "question": "<strong>Case Study:</strong> A linear function is defined by $f(x) = mx + c$. Given $f(1) = 3$ and $f(2) = 5$.<br>(i) Find the values of $m$ and $c$.<br>(ii) Find $f(5)$.<br>(iii) Find $x$ when $f(x) = 11$.",
            "finalAnswer": "(i) m=2, c=1, (ii) 11, (iii) 5",
            "solutionSteps": [
                "(i) $m(1) + c = 3$ and $m(2) + c = 5$.",
                "Subtracting: $m = 2$. Then $2(1) + c = 3 \\implies c = 1$.",
                "$f(x) = 2x + 1$.",
                "(ii) $f(5) = 2(5) + 1 = 11$.",
                "(iii) $2x + 1 = 11 \\implies 2x = 10 \\implies x = 5$."
